  "diagnosis": "the strict-monotone construction WORKED as designed: within every (side, eval-year) cell the recalibrated rank equals the shipped grade rank exactly (rank_preservation_by_cell, 8/8 preserved), so PAVA tie-flattening (the X-ISO failure mode) is eliminated. The pooled Spearman deficit is entirely CROSS-CELL: (a) the four forward-chained maps drift year-to-year, reordering cross-year pairs; (b) the rank metric (expected WAR, side-specific midpoints) interleaves hit vs pit differently than the pooled grade baseline -- the IDENTITY transform already scores below the shipped-grade baseline on this metric (see identity_transform_delta_vs_shipped), so the -0.002 bar requires the recalibration to actively IMPROVE cross-side interleaving, and it instead worsens it (the pit map's top-end compresses toward ~FV 44-45, pushing all top pitchers below top hitters). The single-prior-map sensitivity (zero cross-year drift, per-side preservation exact) still fails condition 2 on cross-side interleaving alone. Condition 3: the FV-35 tier again degrades, but by ~0.001 absolute (0.00265 -> ~0.0035) against a 1e-4 tolerance -- the low-grade bins' effective-grade inversion is slightly too aggressive where the table is already near-perfectly calibrated. The FV45+ calibration gain itself is real and larger than X-ISO's (condition 1 passes with every bucket better; tier-45 gap 0.0946 -> ~0.016, tier-55 0.1616 -> ~0.044).",
